---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About Andrew McLeod" description="Thirty years in brand and marketing. Every shift in the industry. Andrew McLeod, founder of GreaterThan.">

<!-- HERO -->
<section class="hero hero--sub section--indigo">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="about-hero-inner">
      <div class="hero__inner">
        <h1>Thirty years in brand and marketing. Every shift in the industry.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="about-photo">
        <span>Photo</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- BACKGROUND -->
<section class="about-content-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="reveal">Background</h2>
    <p class="reveal d1">Andrew McLeod came to brand and advertising in 1996, when the internet was still new and brand was what you owned, not what you managed. Twenty years at senior strategic level in New Zealand's largest brand and advertising agencies took him through every major shift the industry has had: broadcast, web, digital, social, and now AI and AEO.</p>
    <p class="reveal d2">From 1996 to 2022, the thread was always the same: brand as the foundation. That's where a business's goals meet an audience's needs. Everything else — campaign, channel, content, AI, automation — is expression of that relationship. Without brand at the centre, marketing becomes activity. With it, every dollar compounds.</p>
    <p class="reveal d2">In July 2022, he stepped out of agency to lead GreaterThan as an independent practice.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHY INDEPENDENT -->
<section class="about-content-section section--paper">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="reveal">Why independent consulting</h2>
    <p class="reveal d1">At agency, you're solving for what the agency can sell. As an independent, you're solving for what the business actually needs. The difference is everything.</p>
    <p class="reveal d2">Independence means no inventory to sell, no account team to bill, no pressure to add scope. It means looking at the business honestly and recommending what it actually needs, whether that's a big project or a simple strategic conversation.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- APPROACH -->
<section class="about-content-section" id="approach">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="reveal">Approach</h2>
    <p class="reveal d1">Every engagement begins by reading the business. Where it's heading, who the customers actually are, what the marketing currently delivers against what's needed. The work that follows is shaped by what you find, not by what was expected when you walked in.</p>
    <p class="reveal d2">What doesn't change is the principle: your marketing should serve your business strategy. Not be its own discipline. Not win awards or look modern. Serve what your business is trying to achieve. Everything flows from that.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA -->
<section class="cta-band">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="cta-band__inner">
      <h2>Want to work <em>together</em>?</h2>
      <div class="cta-band__right">
        <span class="cta-band__email">hello@wearegreaterthan.co.nz</span>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--primary-dark">Book a discovery call <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</BaseLayout>
